from bike-slope.replay
# Part of sys-bike: Oreburgh Gate B1F, the westward bike ramp at (27, 13). After a run-up from (32, 13)
# in gear 1 (speed >= 3) the bike jumps from the ramp tile 3 tiles west (JUMP_FARTHER_WEST: 4 px a
# frame for 12 frames) to (24, 13), over the gap at x 25. On the ramp tile B does not change the gear
# (PlayerAvatar_TryCyclingGearChange); after the landing it does. The `bike-jump`/`bike-landed`
# screenshot lines are the browser spec's key beat: mid-jump the player is drawn higher on screen.
warp platinum:MAP_HEADER_OREBURGH_GATE_B1F 32 13 left
until idle
+0 assert state playerState "cycle"
+0 press left
until position 27 13
+0 press b
+1 release b
+0 assert state cyclingGear 1
until position 24 13 30
+0 release left
+0 assert position platinum:MAP_HEADER_OREBURGH_GATE_B1F 24 13
+5 screenshot bike-jump
until idle
+0 screenshot bike-landed
+0 press b
+1 release b
+1 assert state cyclingGear 0
+0 press b
+1 release b
+1 assert state cyclingGear 1
